  ('d37','Chloramphenicol','Kemicetine, Chloromycetin','Amphenicol antibiotic','Typhoid fever, bacterial meningitis (alternative), severe infections where alternatives unsuitable; topical for eye infections','Bone marrow suppression, aplastic anemia (rare, idiosyncratic), grey baby syndrome in neonates, optic neuritis','Warfarin, phenytoin, sulphonylureas, rifampicin (reduced levels)','Neonates/late pregnancy (grey baby syndrome), pre-existing bone marrow depression, porphyria','Adults: 50 mg/kg/day divided every 6 hours (systemic, reserve use). Topical eye drops: apply as directed. Monitor blood counts with systemic use.','C','US-FDA (legacy)',0,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
