  ('d45','Nifedipine','Adalat, Nifedical','Dihydropyridine calcium channel blocker','Hypertension, angina, Raynaud phenomenon; modified-release for hypertension in pregnancy','Ankle edema, flushing, headache, reflex tachycardia, gum hyperplasia','CYP3A4 inhibitors (grapefruit, azoles), beta-blockers, other antihypertensives','Cardiogenic shock, unstable angina, significant aortic stenosis; avoid immediate-release for chronic hypertension','Adults: modified-release 20-30 mg once or twice daily. Avoid short-acting immediate-release for routine hypertension. Swallow MR whole.','C','US-FDA (legacy)',0,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
  ('d46','Atenolol','Tenormin, Aten','Cardioselective beta-blocker','Hypertension, angina, arrhythmias, post-MI','Bradycardia, fatigue, cold extremities, bronchospasm, masked hypoglycemia','Verapamil/diltiazem (heart block), insulin/antidiabetics, NSAIDs, clonidine (rebound)','Asthma/severe COPD, second/third-degree heart block, decompensated heart failure, severe bradycardia','Adults: 25-100 mg once daily. Do not stop abruptly (taper to avoid rebound). Reduce dose in renal impairment.','D','US-FDA (legacy)',0,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
  ('d47','Bisoprolol','Concor, Cardicor','Cardioselective beta-blocker','Hypertension, angina, chronic stable heart failure','Bradycardia, fatigue, dizziness, cold extremities, bronchospasm','Verapamil/diltiazem, amiodarone, insulin/antidiabetics, other rate-limiting drugs','Severe asthma, acute decompensated heart failure, second/third-degree heart block, marked bradycardia/hypotension','Adults: hypertension 5-10 mg once daily. Heart failure: start 1.25 mg daily and titrate slowly. Do not stop abruptly.','C','US-FDA (legacy)',0,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
  ('d48','Carvedilol','Coreg, Dilatrend','Alpha/beta-blocker','Chronic heart failure, hypertension, angina, post-MI LV dysfunction','Dizziness, hypotension, bradycardia, fatigue, weight gain (fluid), bronchospasm','Rate-limiting calcium blockers, digoxin, insulin/antidiabetics, CYP2D6 inhibitors','Severe asthma, acute decompensated heart failure, second/third-degree heart block, severe hepatic impairment','Adults: heart failure start 3.125 mg twice daily with food, double every 2 weeks as tolerated. Take with food to slow absorption.','C','US-FDA (legacy)',0,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
  ('d49','Losartan-Hydrochlorothiazide','Hyzaar, Losacar-H','ARB/thiazide combination','Hypertension not controlled by monotherapy','Dizziness, hyperkalemia or hypokalemia, hyponatremia, hyperuricemia','Lithium, NSAIDs, potassium supplements, other antihypertensives','Pregnancy, anuria, severe renal/hepatic impairment','Adults: 50/12.5 mg once daily, up to 100/25 mg daily. Not for initial therapy. Monitor electrolytes and renal function.','D','US-FDA (legacy)',0,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
  ('d50','Furosemide','Lasix, Frusol','Loop diuretic','Edema in heart failure, renal/hepatic disease, pulmonary edema, resistant hypertension','Hypokalemia, hyponatremia, dehydration, ototoxicity (high IV doses), hyperuricemia, hyperglycemia','Aminoglycosides (ototoxicity), lithium, digoxin (hypokalemia), NSAIDs, antihypertensives','Anuria, severe hypokalemia/hyponatremia, hepatic coma, hypovolemia','Adults: 20-40 mg once or twice daily orally; higher doses in renal impairment. Give early in the day to avoid nocturia. Monitor electrolytes.','C','US-FDA (legacy)',0,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
  ('d51','Spironolactone','Aldactone, Spironol','Potassium-sparing diuretic/aldosterone antagonist','Heart failure, resistant hypertension, ascites, primary hyperaldosteronism, edema','Hyperkalemia, gynecomastia, menstrual irregularity, GI upset','ACE inhibitors/ARBs, potassium supplements, NSAIDs, digoxin, trimethoprim','Hyperkalemia, severe renal impairment, Addison disease, anuria','Adults: 25-100 mg daily. Heart failure: 12.5-25 mg daily. Monitor potassium and renal function closely, especially with ACE inhibitors/ARBs.','C','US-FDA (legacy)',0,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
