VALUES
  ('d104','Omeprazole (GI)','Losec, Omez','Proton pump inhibitor','GERD, peptic ulcer disease, H. pylori eradication, NSAID ulcer prophylaxis','Headache, diarrhea, abdominal pain, hypomagnesemia and B12 deficiency (long term), raised fracture risk','Clopidogrel (reduced activation — avoid), methotrexate, digoxin, azole antifungals','Hypersensitivity; use lowest effective dose long term','Adults: 20-40 mg once daily before breakfast. Review need for long-term use. Prefer pantoprazole if a PPI is needed with clopidogrel.','C','US-FDA (legacy)',1,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
  ('d105','Pantoprazole','Protonix, Pantocid','Proton pump inhibitor','GERD, peptic ulcer, NSAID ulcer prophylaxis; preferred PPI with clopidogrel','Headache, diarrhea, hypomagnesemia (long term), B12 deficiency','Fewer CYP2C19 interactions than omeprazole; methotrexate, atazanavir','Hypersensitivity','Adults: 20-40 mg once daily before food. Suitable where clopidogrel is co-prescribed. Review long-term need.','B','US-FDA (legacy)',0,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
  ('d106','Ranitidine','Zantac, Rantac','H2-receptor antagonist','Dyspepsia, GERD, peptic ulcer (where used)','Headache, dizziness, constipation/diarrhea; note NDMA supply concerns in some markets','Reduced absorption of some drugs needing acid (e.g., ketoconazole)','Hypersensitivity','Adults: 150 mg twice daily or 300 mg at night. Availability varies due to product recalls in some countries; verify local supply.','B','US-FDA (legacy)',1,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
  ('d107','Metoclopramide','Maxolon, Perinorm','Prokinetic/antiemetic (dopamine antagonist)','Nausea and vomiting, gastroparesis, migraine-associated nausea','Extrapyramidal reactions (especially young/elderly), drowsiness, restlessness, tardive dyskinesia (prolonged use)','Antipsychotics (additive extrapyramidal effects), levodopa (antagonism), CNS depressants','GI obstruction/perforation/haemorrhage, phaeochromocytoma, epilepsy, Parkinson disease; limit to 5 days','Adults: 10 mg up to 3 times daily, maximum 5 days. Avoid in young adults where possible (dystonia risk). Reduce in renal impairment.','B','US-FDA (legacy)',0,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
  ('d108','Ondansetron','Zofran, Emeset','5-HT3 receptor antagonist antiemetic','Chemotherapy/radiotherapy-induced and post-operative nausea and vomiting','Headache, constipation, QT prolongation, flushing','QT-prolonging drugs, apomorphine (avoid — severe hypotension), tramadol','Congenital long QT syndrome; concurrent apomorphine','Adults: 4-8 mg every 8-12 hours. Caution with other QT-prolonging drugs and electrolyte disturbance. Reduce max dose in hepatic impairment.','B','US-FDA (legacy)',0,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
  ('d109','Loperamide','Imodium, Lopamide','Antimotility antidiarrheal','Symptomatic relief of acute and chronic diarrhea (non-infective)','Constipation, abdominal cramps, dizziness; cardiac events at very high (abuse) doses','QT-prolonging drugs at high doses, CYP3A4 inhibitors','Acute dysentery (blood in stool with fever), bacterial enterocolitis, children under 12 without advice, active ulcerative colitis flare','Adults: 4 mg initially then 2 mg after each loose stool, max 16 mg/day. Do not use if there is blood in stool or high fever. Rehydrate with ORS.','C','US-FDA (legacy)',1,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
  ('d110','Hyoscine Butylbromide','Buscopan','Antimuscarinic antispasmodic','Abdominal cramps, IBS-type spasm, biliary/renal colic (adjunct)','Dry mouth, blurred vision, tachycardia, constipation, urinary retention','Other anticholinergics, antihistamines, tricyclics','Narrow-angle glaucoma, myasthenia gravis, GI obstruction, urinary retention, tachyarrhythmias','Adults: 10-20 mg up to 4 times daily. Short-term symptomatic use. Avoid in the conditions listed above.','C','US-FDA (legacy)',1,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
  ('d111','Bisacodyl','Dulcolax','Stimulant laxative','Constipation, bowel preparation','Abdominal cramps, diarrhea, electrolyte disturbance with overuse','Antacids/milk (avoid within 1 hour of enteric-coated tablets), diuretics','Intestinal obstruction, acute abdomen, severe dehydration','Adults: 5-10 mg at night orally. Do not crush/chew enteric-coated tablets. Short-term use; increase fluids and fibre.','C','US-FDA (legacy)',1,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
  ('d112','Lactulose','Duphalac, Cephulac','Osmotic laxative','Constipation, hepatic encephalopathy','Flatulence, abdominal cramps, diarrhea (excess dose)','Few significant interactions','Galactosemia, intestinal obstruction','Adults: constipation 15 mL twice daily, adjust to response; hepatic encephalopathy higher doses titrated to 2-3 soft stools daily. Effect may take 48 hours.','B','US-FDA (legacy)',1,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
  ('d113','Oral Rehydration Salts (low osmolarity)','ORS, WHO ORS','Electrolyte replacement','Prevention and treatment of dehydration from diarrhea and vomiting','Vomiting if taken too quickly; hypernatremia if wrongly reconstituted','None significant','Severe dehydration/shock (needs IV fluids), paralytic ileus, persistent vomiting','Dissolve one sachet in 1 litre of clean/boiled cooled water; give frequent small sips. Discard after 24 hours. Combine with zinc in childhood diarrhea.','A','US-FDA (legacy)',1,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
  ('d114','Zinc Sulfate','Zinc, Zincovit (component)','Mineral supplement','Adjunct in childhood diarrhea (reduces duration/severity), zinc deficiency','Nausea, vomiting, metallic taste, abdominal discomfort','Reduces absorption of quinolones and tetracyclines; iron/calcium','Hypersensitivity','Children with diarrhea: 20 mg daily (10 mg if under 6 months) for 10-14 days alongside ORS. Give with or after food.','C','US-FDA (legacy)',1,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
  ('d115','Mebeverine','Colofac','Antispasmodic (musculotropic)','Irritable bowel syndrome — abdominal pain and spasm','Rare: rash, dizziness; generally well tolerated','Few significant interactions','Paralytic ileus; hypersensitivity','Adults: 135 mg three times daily, 20 minutes before meals, or 200 mg modified-release twice daily. Symptomatic relief for IBS.','C','US-FDA (legacy)',1,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL);

