VALUES
  ('d116','Ferrous Sulfate','Ferrograd, Fersolate','Oral iron supplement','Iron-deficiency anemia, prevention in pregnancy','Constipation, black stools, nausea, epigastric pain','Tetracyclines/quinolones (reduced absorption), antacids, levothyroxine, calcium','Iron-overload states (haemochromatosis, thalassaemia without deficiency), hypersensitivity','Adults: 200 mg (65 mg elemental iron) 1-3 times daily. Take with vitamin C to aid absorption; separate from tea/antacids. Stools turn black (normal).','A','US-FDA (legacy)',1,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
  ('d117','Folic Acid','Folvite, Folicare','Vitamin (B9)','Prevention of neural tube defects, folate-deficiency anemia, adjunct in sickle cell and haemolytic anemias','Rare: nausea, rash','Phenytoin (reduced levels), sulfasalazine, methotrexate (antagonist)','Should not be used alone in untreated vitamin B12 deficiency (masks it)','Pregnancy prevention: 400 mcg daily pre-conception and first trimester (5 mg if high risk). Sickle cell: 5 mg daily. Deficiency: 5 mg daily.','A','US-FDA (legacy)',1,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
  ('d118','Vitamin B Complex','Becosules, Neurobion','Vitamin supplement','Prevention/treatment of B-vitamin deficiencies, peripheral neuropathy (adjunct), general supplementation','Rare: nausea; bright yellow urine (riboflavin)','High-dose B6 with levodopa (reduced effect), phenytoin','Hypersensitivity','Adults: one tablet daily or as directed. Bright yellow urine is harmless. Not a substitute for a balanced diet.','A','US-FDA (legacy)',1,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
  ('d119','Vitamin C (Ascorbic Acid)','Redoxon, Limcee','Vitamin supplement','Vitamin C deficiency/scurvy, adjunct to enhance iron absorption','Rare at normal doses; high doses may cause GI upset and kidney stones','Enhances iron absorption; high doses may affect some lab tests','Hypersensitivity; caution in oxalate kidney stones and haemochromatosis','Adults: 100-1000 mg daily. Often taken with iron to improve absorption. Avoid very high chronic doses.','A','US-FDA (legacy)',1,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
  ('d120','Vitamin D3 (Cholecalciferol)','Calcirol, D-Cure','Vitamin supplement','Vitamin D deficiency, rickets/osteomalacia prevention, adjunct in osteoporosis','Hypercalcemia and hypercalciuria with excessive doses','Thiazides (hypercalcemia), reduced absorption with orlistat/cholestyramine','Hypercalcemia, vitamin D toxicity, some granulomatous diseases','Adults: 800-2000 IU daily for maintenance; higher loading doses for deficiency per protocol. Take with a fat-containing meal.','A','US-FDA (legacy)',1,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
  ('d121','Calcium Carbonate','Calcichew, Shelcal','Mineral supplement/antacid','Calcium supplementation, osteoporosis adjunct, dietary deficiency, antacid','Constipation, bloating, hypercalcemia (excess), kidney stones','Reduces absorption of levothyroxine, tetracyclines, quinolones, iron','Hypercalcemia, severe hypercalciuria, calcium kidney stones','Adults: 500-1000 mg elemental calcium daily in divided doses with food. Separate from thyroid/iron/antibiotic doses by 2-4 hours.','C','US-FDA (legacy)',1,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
  ('d122','Hydroxyurea (Hydroxycarbamide)','Hydrea, Siklos','Antineoplastic/disease-modifying agent','Sickle cell disease (reduces crises and acute chest syndrome), myeloproliferative disorders','Myelosuppression, nausea, skin/nail changes, leg ulcers, teratogenicity','Other myelosuppressants, antiretrovirals (didanosine/stavudine), live vaccines','Pregnancy, severe bone marrow suppression, breastfeeding','Sickle cell: start 15 mg/kg once daily, titrate by response and blood counts (specialist supervision). Requires regular blood count monitoring. Effective contraception needed.','D','US-FDA (legacy)',0,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
  ('d123','Penicillin V (sickle cell prophylaxis)','Pen V','Oral penicillin','Pneumococcal infection prophylaxis in children with sickle cell disease','Nausea, diarrhea, rash, hypersensitivity','Warfarin, methotrexate','Penicillin hypersensitivity','Children with sickle cell: 125 mg twice daily (under 5 yr) or 250 mg twice daily (5 yr and over), typically from a few months of age. Adherence is critical.','B','US-FDA (legacy)',0,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
  ('d124','Multivitamin/Multimineral','Centrum, Supradyn','Nutritional supplement','General micronutrient supplementation, convalescence, dietary gaps','Rare: GI upset; risk of overdose if combined with other supplements','May affect absorption of some drugs (iron, calcium content)','Iron-overload disorders (if iron-containing); avoid duplicating individual supplements','Adults: one tablet daily with food. Not a replacement for a balanced diet; avoid combining multiple products with overlapping vitamins A/D/iron.','A','US-FDA (legacy)',1,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
  ('d125','Ferrous Sulfate-Folic Acid','Fefol, Ferrofol','Iron/folate combination','Prevention and treatment of iron and folate deficiency in pregnancy','Constipation, black stools, nausea','Tetracyclines/quinolones, antacids, levothyroxine','Iron overload states; untreated B12 deficiency (folate masks it)','Pregnancy: one tablet daily (typically ferrous salt with 400 mcg-5 mg folic acid) per antenatal protocol. Take with vitamin C; separate from tea/antacids.','A','US-FDA (legacy)',1,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL);

