VALUES
  ('d126','Combined Oral Contraceptive (Ethinylestradiol-Levonorgestrel)','Microgynon, Lo-Femenal','Combined hormonal contraceptive','Contraception, menstrual regulation, dysmenorrhea','Nausea, breast tenderness, breakthrough bleeding, mood changes, raised VTE risk','Enzyme-inducers (rifampicin, carbamazepine, some ARVs — reduced efficacy), lamotrigine','History of VTE/thrombophilia, migraine with aura, smokers over 35, uncontrolled hypertension, breast cancer, active liver disease, <6 weeks postpartum if breastfeeding','Adults: one tablet daily for 21 days then 7-day break (or continuous per product). Use backup if a dose is missed >24 h or during enzyme-inducer use.','X','US-FDA (legacy)',0,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
  ('d127','Progestogen-only Pill (Levonorgestrel/Norethisterone)','Microlut, Noriday','Progestogen-only contraceptive','Contraception (suitable when estrogen contraindicated, including breastfeeding)','Irregular bleeding, headache, breast tenderness, acne','Enzyme-inducers (rifampicin, carbamazepine, some ARVs)','Current breast cancer, active liver disease, undiagnosed vaginal bleeding','Adults: one tablet daily at the same time with no break; traditional POPs require a strict 3-hour window (12 hours for desogestrel). Use backup if late.','X','US-FDA (legacy)',0,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
  ('d128','Medroxyprogesterone Acetate (Depot)','Depo-Provera','Injectable progestogen contraceptive','Long-acting contraception (3-monthly)','Irregular bleeding/amenorrhea, weight gain, delayed return of fertility, reversible bone density loss','Enzyme-inducers (efficacy less affected than pills), aminoglutethimide','Current breast cancer, undiagnosed vaginal bleeding, active thromboembolic disease','Adults: 150 mg IM every 12 weeks. Counsel on bleeding changes and delayed fertility return. Not affected by GI upset.','X','US-FDA (legacy)',0,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
  ('d129','Levonorgestrel (Emergency Contraception)','Postinor-2, Plan B','Emergency contraceptive','Emergency contraception after unprotected intercourse','Nausea, irregular bleeding, headache, fatigue, delayed period','Enzyme-inducers (reduce efficacy — consider copper IUD or double dose)','Pregnancy (ineffective, not harmful); severe hypersensitivity','Adults: 1.5 mg as a single dose as soon as possible within 72 hours (efficacy falls with time). Available OTC in many settings. Not for regular use.','X','US-FDA (legacy)',1,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
  ('d130','Misoprostol','Cytotec, Misoclear','Prostaglandin E1 analogue','Postpartum hemorrhage prevention/treatment, medical abortion (with mifepristone), labor induction, NSAID ulcer prevention','Diarrhea, abdominal cramps, fever/chills, uterine hyperstimulation','Magnesium antacids (worsen diarrhea)','Pregnancy when used for non-obstetric indications (ulcer prophylaxis); caution/appropriate supervision for obstetric use','Doses vary sharply by indication (route and mcg differ) — MUST follow a specific protocol under clinical supervision. PPH prevention commonly 600 mcg orally after birth.','X','US-FDA (legacy)',0,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
  ('d131','Oxytocin','Syntocinon, Pitocin','Uterotonic hormone','Induction/augmentation of labor, prevention and treatment of postpartum hemorrhage','Uterine hyperstimulation, hypotension, water intoxication (prolonged infusion), nausea','Prostaglandins (additive uterotonic effect), vasoconstrictors','Hypertonic uterus, fetal distress where delivery not imminent, mechanical obstruction to delivery','PPH prevention: 10 IU IM after delivery. Labor: IV infusion titrated under monitoring. Store per cold-chain; hospital/skilled-birth use.','X','US-FDA (legacy)',0,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
  ('d132','Clotrimazole (vaginal)','Canesten','Imidazole antifungal (topical)','Vulvovaginal candidiasis (thrush)','Local burning, itching, irritation','May damage latex condoms/diaphragms','Hypersensitivity; first trimester (use per advice)','Adults: 500 mg pessary as a single dose at night, or 100 mg nightly for 6 nights; plus cream for vulval symptoms. Complete the course.','B','US-FDA (legacy)',1,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
  ('d133','Fluconazole (vaginal candidiasis)','Diflucan, Forcan','Triazole antifungal','Vaginal candidiasis (single-dose oral), other candidal infections','Nausea, headache, abdominal pain, raised liver enzymes, QT prolongation (higher doses)','Warfarin, statins, sulphonylureas, QT-prolonging drugs; many CYP interactions','Pregnancy (avoid high/repeated doses), concurrent QT-prolonging drugs','Vaginal candidiasis: 150 mg orally as a single dose. Avoid in pregnancy where topical azoles are preferred. Check interactions.','D','US-FDA (legacy)',0,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
  ('d134','Tranexamic Acid','Cyklokapron, Femstrual','Antifibrinolytic','Heavy menstrual bleeding, trauma/surgical hemorrhage, postpartum hemorrhage (adjunct)','Nausea, diarrhea, dizziness; rare thromboembolism','Combined hormonal contraceptives (theoretical thrombosis risk), factor concentrates','Active thromboembolic disease, history of VTE, severe renal impairment, seizure history (high IV doses)','Menorrhagia: 1 g three times daily for up to 4 days during menstruation. PPH/trauma: 1 g IV per protocol. Reduce in renal impairment.','B','US-FDA (legacy)',0,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
  ('d135','Mifepristone','Mifegyne','Antiprogestogen','Medical termination of pregnancy (with misoprostol), cervical priming — regulated use only','Bleeding, cramping, nausea, fatigue','NSAIDs (theoretical), CYP3A4 inducers/inhibitors, corticosteroids (reduced effect)','Suspected ectopic pregnancy, chronic adrenal failure, inherited porphyrias, severe uncontrolled asthma; regulated indication','Used only within an approved, supervised protocol with misoprostol. Dosing and eligibility per national guidelines and law. Not for self-administration.','X','US-FDA (legacy)',0,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL);

