VALUES
  ('d136','Hydrocortisone (topical)','Dermacort, Cortaid','Mild topical corticosteroid','Eczema, dermatitis, insect bites, mild inflammatory skin conditions','Skin thinning, telangiectasia with prolonged use; local irritation','Minimal systemic interaction with short topical use','Untreated skin infections (bacterial/fungal/viral), rosacea, perioral dermatitis, broken skin (caution)','Apply a thin layer 1-2 times daily to affected areas for up to 7 days. Avoid the face and skin folds for prolonged periods. Not for infected skin.','C','US-FDA (legacy)',1,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
  ('d137','Betamethasone (topical)','Betnovate, Diprosone','Potent topical corticosteroid','Moderate-to-severe eczema, psoriasis, dermatoses unresponsive to milder steroids','Skin atrophy, striae, telangiectasia, systemic absorption on large areas','Minimal with correct use','Untreated skin infections, rosacea, perioral dermatitis, extensive use in children','Apply thinly once or twice daily for a limited period. Avoid face/flexures unless directed. Step down to a milder steroid when improving.','C','US-FDA (legacy)',0,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
  ('d138','Clotrimazole (topical)','Canesten, Candid','Imidazole antifungal (topical)','Tinea (ringworm, athlete''s foot), cutaneous candidiasis, pityriasis versicolor','Local burning, irritation, redness','Minimal','Hypersensitivity','Apply 2-3 times daily and continue for 1-2 weeks after lesions clear to prevent relapse. Keep the area clean and dry.','B','US-FDA (legacy)',1,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
  ('d139','Permethrin','Lyclear, Nix','Topical antiparasitic (pyrethroid)','Scabies, head lice','Local itching, burning, redness (may transiently worsen after treatment)','Minimal','Hypersensitivity to pyrethroids/chrysanthemums','Scabies: apply 5% cream to the whole body (neck down; include scalp in young children), wash off after 8-12 hours; repeat after 7 days. Treat close contacts.','B','US-FDA (legacy)',1,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
  ('d140','Benzyl Benzoate','Ascabiol','Topical antiparasitic','Scabies, lice (where permethrin unavailable)','Skin irritation, burning (especially genitals/broken skin)','Minimal','Broken/inflamed skin, young infants (use with care/dilution)','Apply to the whole body below the neck, leave for 24 hours, then wash off; often repeated. Can be irritant — dilute for children per guidance.','C','US-FDA (legacy)',1,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
  ('d141','Silver Sulfadiazine','Flamazine, Silverex','Topical antibacterial','Prevention/treatment of infection in burns and wounds','Local reactions, transient leukopenia, argyria (prolonged extensive use)','Enzymatic wound debriding agents (inactivated), topical proteolytics','Pregnancy near term, premature infants and neonates (kernicterus risk), sulphonamide hypersensitivity','Apply a 3-5 mm layer to clean burn once or twice daily under dressing. Avoid in late pregnancy and neonates.','C','US-FDA (legacy)',0,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
  ('d142','Benzoyl Peroxide','Benzac, Panoxyl','Topical keratolytic/antibacterial','Mild-to-moderate acne vulgaris','Dryness, peeling, redness, stinging; bleaches fabric/hair','Topical retinoids (use at different times), other irritants','Hypersensitivity','Apply 2.5-5% once or twice daily to affected areas after washing. Start low strength/frequency to limit irritation. May bleach clothing/bedding.','C','US-FDA (legacy)',1,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
  ('d143','Calamine Lotion','Calamine','Topical antipruritic/protectant','Itching, mild sunburn, insect bites, chickenpox rash','Rare; occasional dryness','None significant','Hypersensitivity','Apply to affected skin as needed with cotton wool. Soothes itching; for symptomatic relief only.','A','US-FDA (legacy)',1,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL);

