VALUES
  ('d144','Chloramphenicol (eye)','Chloromycetin eye, Optrex Infected Eye','Topical ophthalmic antibiotic','Bacterial conjunctivitis, superficial eye infections','Transient stinging, local allergy; very rarely bone marrow effects','Minimal topical','Hypersensitivity; personal/family history of blood dyscrasia (caution)','Drops: 1 drop every 2 hours initially then reduce; ointment at night. Continue for 48 hours after healing. Discard after the recommended in-use period.','C','US-FDA (legacy)',1,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
  ('d145','Ciprofloxacin (eye/ear)','Ciloxan, Ciplox','Topical fluoroquinolone','Bacterial conjunctivitis, corneal ulcers, otitis externa','Local irritation, transient blurring, white corneal precipitate (eye)','Minimal topical','Hypersensitivity to quinolones','Eye: 1-2 drops every 2-4 hours, reducing as it improves. Ear: 2-4 drops twice daily. Do not touch the dropper to the eye/ear.','C','US-FDA (legacy)',0,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
  ('d146','Timolol (eye)','Timoptol','Topical beta-blocker (ophthalmic)','Open-angle glaucoma, ocular hypertension','Local stinging; systemic beta-blockade (bradycardia, bronchospasm) via absorption','Systemic beta-blockers, verapamil/diltiazem','Asthma/severe COPD, bradycardia, heart block, uncompensated heart failure','1 drop of 0.25-0.5% into the affected eye(s) twice daily. Punctal occlusion reduces systemic absorption. Caution in respiratory/cardiac disease.','C','US-FDA (legacy)',0,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
  ('d147','Xylometazoline (nasal)','Otrivin','Topical nasal decongestant','Short-term relief of nasal congestion (colds, rhinitis, sinusitis)','Local stinging/dryness, rebound congestion with overuse (rhinitis medicamentosa)','MAOIs (caution)','Use beyond 5-7 days, children under 6 (0.05% for 6-12), narrow-angle glaucoma','Adults: 1 spray/drop of 0.1% per nostril 2-3 times daily for no more than 5-7 days to avoid rebound congestion.','C','US-FDA (legacy)',1,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
  ('d148','Betahistine','Serc, Vertin','Histamine analogue','Meniere disease — vertigo, tinnitus, hearing loss','Nausea, dyspepsia, headache','Antihistamines (theoretical antagonism)','Phaeochromocytoma; caution in active peptic ulcer and asthma','Adults: 16 mg three times daily initially, then 24-48 mg/day maintenance, with or after food.','C','US-FDA (legacy)',0,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL),
  ('d149','Sodium Chloride 0.9% (nasal/eye)','Normal saline drops','Isotonic saline','Nasal irrigation, eye rinsing, moistening dry mucosa, infant nasal congestion','None significant','None','None significant','Use as drops or spray as needed. Safe for infants and pregnancy. For irrigation/rinsing and symptomatic relief.','A','US-FDA (legacy)',1,0,'WHO EML 2023; Ghana STG 2017 (AI-drafted — pending pharmacist review)','https://list.essentialmeds.org/',NULL,NULL);

